        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How do I connect my Apple Watch to a Planet Fitness treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Find a treadmill whose console shows "Connects to Apple Watch". On the watch, go to Settings, then Workout, and turn on Detect Gym Equipment. Hold the watch display within a few centimeters of the console's reader until it taps and beeps, then press Start on the treadmill, and press Stop on the treadmill to end.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Do all Planet Fitness treadmills have Apple GymKit?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. GymKit depends on the console, and Planet Fitness clubs replace equipment on their own five-to-nine-year cycles, so support varies by club and by machine. Life Fitness names GymKit as one of the additions on the SL-Console it supplies for Planet Fitness, compared with the older C-Console. The logo on the console is the reliable test.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Why won't my Apple Watch connect to the treadmill at Planet Fitness?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              First check the console has the "Connects to Apple Watch" logo. Then switch Detect Gym Equipment off and on in the watch's Workout settings, make sure Low Power Mode is off and Bluetooth is on, and hold the watch display close to the reader. If it still fails, open the Workout app first and tap again, or try another machine and tell staff.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does the Planet Fitness app work on Apple Watch?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Its App Store listing shows it as an iPhone-only app, with no Apple Watch app (checked November 2026). It can sync your activity with Apple Health, and its digital Club Pass for check-in is on the phone. Pairing your watch with a treadmill is handled by Apple's GymKit, not the Planet Fitness app.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What brand of treadmill does Planet Fitness use?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Planet Fitness sells "Planet Fitness-branded" equipment to its franchisees and says it buys it from third-party manufacturers it does not name in its annual report. Life Fitness's support site documents consoles made for Planet Fitness, and members report Matrix machines too. Clubs differ, so check the badge on the machine.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How do I track a Planet Fitness treadmill run without GymKit?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Start an Indoor Run or Indoor Walk in the watch's Workout app as you start the belt, let your arms swing naturally, and note the console's distance before it resets. Correct the distance afterwards where your watchOS version or Strava allows. Calibrating the watch with about 20 minutes of outdoor walking or running improves its indoor estimates.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
